<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Athinkhaya</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1310</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Athinkhaya was the eldest of the three brothers who founded the Myinsaing regime in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> in the late 13th century. Commanders under the last Pagan kings, he and his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yazathingyan">Yazathingyan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thihathu">Thihathu</a> governed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyaukse">Kyaukse</a> district, overthrew King Kyawswa in 1297 and withstood a Yuan Mongol army in 1300 to 1301. He ruled from Myinsaing until his death in 1310.</p></div>
